    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced, supporting a Hold rather than a directional call. The bull case rests on a strong structural uptrend (+24.3% over 60 days, price above rising 10 EMA/50 SMA/200 SMA) and fortress cash generation ($62.6B operating cash flow, $61B returned to shareholders). However, the bear's counterpoints carry real weight: the June 21 session showed the highest volume of the period (241.8M shares) on a down day \u2014 a distribution signature \u2014 the stock has failed to reclaim $214 for seven days and made no higher high for 16 days, MACD has confirmed a bearish crossover, and RSI has deteriorated from 79.58 to 61.70. The realistic risk/reward is asymmetric to the downside (~2:1) at $208.63 given the 9.4% drawdown to the 50 SMA at $189 if $203.6 breaks. With the income statement data unavailable in this historical window, the fundamental debate is unresolved. The prudent stance is to maintain existing positions, avoid chasing at $208, and wait for either a pullback to the $203-204 zone or a confirmed breakout above $218 on volume.\n\n**Entry Price**: 203.5\n\n**Stop Loss**: 203.6\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-slightly-underweight allocation relative to benchmark; do not add new exposure at current levels\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
